# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module functions (generic API)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Wraps `value` in a present `maybe T`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `value`: the payload to box.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(value)`, owned by the caller.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as maybe int is calling oracle.some_of with 42
## ```
weave some_of shard T with value as T into maybe T:
    return some value

## Returns an empty `maybe T`. The type argument must be explicit.
##
## ## Retorno
## `maybe none` with element type `T`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var m as maybe int is calling oracle.none_of of int
## ```
weave none_of shard T into maybe T:
    return maybe none

## Returns `true` when `m` holds a value.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to inspect. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when present, `false` when empty. Functional alias of `m.is_some`.
weave is_some_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into bool:
    return m is present

## Returns `true` when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to inspect. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when empty, `false` when present. Functional alias of `m.is_none`.
weave is_none_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into bool:
    return not (m is present)

## Returns the payload of `m`, or panics with `"Unwrapped none maybe"` when `m`
## is empty.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to extract from. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the payload.
weave unwrap_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into T:
    if v as T is m:
        return v
    calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped none maybe"
    let owns as maybe T is m
    return owns.value

## Returns the payload of `m`, or `fallback` when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `fallback`: the `T` returned when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## The payload, or `fallback`.
weave unwrap_or_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, fallback as T into T:
    if v as T is m:
        return v
    return fallback

## Returns the payload of `m`, or the result of invoking `f` when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a zero-argument weave producing the `T` to use as fallback.
##
## ## Retorno
## The payload, or `f()`; `f` is only invoked when `m` is empty.
weave unwrap_or_else_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, f as weave into T into T:
    if v as T is m:
        return v
    return calling f

## Returns the payload of `m`, or panics with `message` when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `message`: the text passed to `spark.panic` when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the payload.
weave expect_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, message as string into T:
    if v as T is m:
        return v
    calling spark.panic with message
    let owns as maybe T is m
    return owns.value

## Alias of `unwrap_or_maybe`: the payload of `m`, or `fallback`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `fallback`: the `T` returned when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## The payload, or `fallback`.
weave value_or_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, fallback as T into T:
    if v as T is m:
        return v
    return fallback

## Applies `f` to the payload of `m`, keeping the container.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to transform. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `T` into `U`; called only when `m` is present.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `some(f(v))` when present, `maybe none` when empty.
weave map_maybe shard T and U with m as maybe T, f as weave with x as T into U into maybe U:
    if v as T is m:
        return some (calling f with v)
    return maybe none

## Keeps the payload of `m` only when `predicate` returns `true`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to filter. Borrowed.
## - `predicate`: a weave from `T` into `bool`; called only when `m` is present.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `some(v)` when the predicate accepts, `maybe none` otherwise.
weave filter_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, predicate as weave with x as T into bool into maybe T:
    if v as T is m:
        if calling predicate with v:
            return some v
    return maybe none

## Chains `f` over the payload of `m` (so containers never nest).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to transform. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `T` into `maybe U`; called only when `m` is present.
##
## ## Retorno
## The `maybe U` rebuilt from `f`'s payload, or `maybe none`.
weave and_then_maybe shard T and U with m as maybe T, f as weave with x as T into maybe U into maybe U:
    if v as T is m:
        let nxt as maybe U is calling f with v
        if w as U is nxt:
            return some w
    return maybe none

## Returns `m` when it has a value; otherwise `fallback`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the first optional. Borrowed.
## - `fallback`: the optional consulted when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt container holding whichever payload was found.
weave or_else_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, fallback as maybe T into maybe T:
    if v as T is m:
        return some v
    if w as T is fallback:
        return some w
    return maybe none

## Returns `right` only when `left` has a value.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `left`: the optional that gates the result. Borrowed.
## - `right`: the optional whose payload is kept.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `some` with `right`'s payload when both are present, `maybe none`
## otherwise.
weave and_maybe shard T with left as maybe T, right as maybe T into maybe T:
    if left is present:
        if w as T is right:
            return some w
    return maybe none

## Returns `left` when it has a value; otherwise `right`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `left`: the first optional. Borrowed.
## - `right`: the optional consulted when `left` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt container holding the first payload available.
weave or_maybe shard T with left as maybe T, right as maybe T into maybe T:
    if v as T is left:
        return some v
    if w as T is right:
        return some w
    return maybe none

## Promotes `m` to `result of T to string`, using `error_value` as the error.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to promote. Borrowed.
## - `error_value`: the error stored when `m` is empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok(payload)` when present, `err(error_value)` when empty.
weave to_result_maybe shard T with m as maybe T, error_value as string into result of T to string:
    if v as T is m:
        return calling ok_of with v
    return calling err_of with error_value

## Returns a one-element list with the payload of `m`, or an empty list.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A newly allocated owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
weave to_list_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into list of T:
    if v as T is m:
        return [v]
    return list of T

## Renders `m` as `"some(v)"` or `"none"`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to render. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The rendered string.
weave describe_optional shard T with m as maybe T into string:
    if v as T is m:
        return "some({v})"
    return "none"

## Alias of `to_list_maybe`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A newly allocated owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
weave iter_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into list of T:
    if v as T is m:
        return [v]
    return list of T

## Combines two present optionals into a `Pair of T and U`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `left`: the first optional. Borrowed.
## - `right`: the second optional. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(Pair)` when both are present, `maybe none` otherwise. The `Pair` is
## owned by the caller.
weave zip_maybe shard T and U with left as maybe T, right as maybe U into maybe Pair of T and U:
    if a as T is left:
        if b as U is right:
            var out as Pair of T and U with:
                set .first is a
                set .second is b
            return some out
    return maybe none

## Re-boxes the payload of `m` in a fresh container.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `m`: the optional to re-box. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(v)` when present, `maybe none` when empty; it cannot collapse
## `maybe maybe U`.
weave flatten_maybe shard T with m as maybe T into maybe T:
    if inner as T is m:
        return some inner
    return maybe none

## Returns `true` when `r` represents success.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to classify. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` for `ok`, `false` for `err`. Functional alias of `r.is_ok`.
weave is_ok_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into bool:
    return r.is_ok

## Returns `true` when `r` represents an error.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to classify. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` for `err`, `false` for `ok`. Functional alias of `r.is_err`.
weave is_err_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into bool:
    return not r.is_ok

## Returns the success payload of `r`, or panics with `"Unwrapped err result"`
## when `r` is `err`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the success payload.
weave unwrap_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return r.value
    calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped err result"
    let owns as result of T to E is r
    return owns.value

## Returns the error of `r`, or panics with `"unwrap_err on ok result"` when `r`
## is `ok`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the stored error.
weave unwrap_err_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into E:
    if r.is_ok:
        calling spark.panic with "unwrap_err on ok result"
    return r.error

## Returns the success payload of `r`, or `fallback` when `r` is `err`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `fallback`: the `T` returned for `err`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The success payload, or `fallback`.
weave unwrap_or_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E, fallback as T into T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return r.value
    return fallback

## Returns the success payload of `r`, or `f(error)` when `r` is `err`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `E` into `T`, called only for `err`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The success payload, or the value produced by `f`.
weave unwrap_or_else_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E, f as weave with x as E into T into T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return r.value
    return calling f with r.error

## Returns the success payload of `r`, or panics with `message` when `r` is
## `err`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `message`: the text passed to `spark.panic` for `err`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the success payload.
weave expect_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E, message as string into T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return r.value
    calling spark.panic with message
    let owns as result of T to E is r
    return owns.value

## Returns the error of `r`, or panics with `message` when `r` is `ok`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to extract from. Borrowed.
## - `message`: the text passed to `spark.panic` for `ok`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A copy of the stored error.
weave expect_err_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E, message as string into E:
    if r.is_ok:
        calling spark.panic with message
    return r.error

## Applies `f` to the success payload of `r`, propagating the error.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to transform. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `T` into `U`, called only for `ok`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `result of U to E`: `ok(f(v))` or the original error.
weave map_result shard T and E and U with r as result of T to E, f as weave with x as T into U into result of U to E:
    if r.is_ok:
        return calling ok_of with (calling f with r.value)
    return calling err_of with r.error

## Applies `f` to the error of `r`, propagating success.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to transform. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `E` into `F`, called only for `err`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `result of T to F`: `err(f(e))` or the original success.
weave map_err_result shard T and E and F with r as result of T to E, f as weave with x as E into F into result of T to F:
    if r.is_ok:
        return calling ok_of with r.value
    return calling err_of with (calling f with r.error)

## Chains `f` over the success payload of `r`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to chain from. Borrowed.
## - `f`: a weave from `T` into `result of U to E`, called only for `ok`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The rebuilt result produced by `f`, or the original error.
weave and_then_result shard T and E and U with r as result of T to E, f as weave with x as T into result of U to E into result of U to E:
    if r.is_ok:
        let nxt as result of U to E is calling f with r.value
        if nxt.is_ok:
            return calling ok_of with nxt.value
        return calling err_of with nxt.error
    return calling err_of with r.error

## Returns `r` when it is `ok`; otherwise `fallback` (same error type).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the first result. Borrowed.
## - `fallback`: the result consulted when `r` is `err`.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt result holding whichever outcome was chosen.
weave or_else_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E, fallback as result of T to E into result of T to E:
    if r.is_ok:
        return calling ok_of with r.value
    if fallback.is_ok:
        return calling ok_of with fallback.value
    return calling err_of with fallback.error

## Discards the error of `r`: a `maybe` with the success payload.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(v)` for `ok`, `maybe none` for `err`.
weave ok_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into maybe T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return some r.value
    return maybe none

## Discards the success of `r`: a `maybe` with the error.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(e)` for `err`, `maybe none` for `ok`.
weave err_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into maybe E:
    if r.is_ok:
        return maybe none
    return some r.error

## Alias of `ok_result`: the success payload as a `maybe T`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some(v)` for `ok`, `maybe none` for `err`.
weave to_maybe_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into maybe T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return some r.value
    return maybe none

## Returns a one-element list with the success payload of `r`, or an empty list.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to convert. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A newly allocated owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
weave to_list_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into list of T:
    if r.is_ok:
        return [r.value]
    return list of T

## Renders `r` as `"ok(v)"` or `"err(e)"`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: the result to render. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The rendered string.
weave describe_result shard T and E with r as result of T to E into string:
    if r.is_ok:
        return "ok({r.value})"
    return "err({r.error})"

## Returns `true` when every element of `ms` is present.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ms`: the list of optionals to scan. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` for an empty list (vacuous truth) and for a list whose elements are all
## present, `false` as soon as one is empty.
weave all_present shard T with ms as list of maybe T into bool:
    for m in ms:
        if not (m is present):
            return false
    return true

## Returns the first payload present in `ms`, or `maybe none`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ms`: the list of optionals to scan, in order. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A rebuilt `some(v)` for the first present element, `maybe none` when every
## element is empty.
weave first_present shard T with ms as list of maybe T into maybe T:
    for m in ms:
        if v as T is m:
            return some v
    return maybe none

## Returns `true` when at least one element of `ms` is present.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `ms`: the list of optionals to scan. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` on the first present element, `false` when every element is empty.
weave any_present shard T with ms as list of maybe T into bool:
    for m in ms:
        if m is present:
            return true
    return false

## Gathers the success payloads of `rs`, in order.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `rs`: the list of results to scan. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A newly allocated owned `list of T` with one entry per `ok`, in order; release
## it with `banish`.
weave collect_ok shard T and E with rs as list of result of T to E into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    for r in rs:
        if r.is_ok:
            calling out.push with r.value
    return out

## Gathers the errors of `rs`, in order.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `rs`: the list of results to scan. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A newly allocated owned `list of E` with one entry per `err`, in order;
## release it with `banish`.
weave collect_err shard T and E with rs as list of result of T to E into list of E:
    var out as list of E is list of E
    for r in rs:
        if not r.is_ok:
            calling out.push with r.error
    return out

## Splits `rs` into a `Pair` of successes and errors.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `rs`: the list of results to partition. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## A `Pair` whose `first` is the owned `list of T` of successes (in order) and
## whose `second` is the owned `list of E` of errors (in order). The caller
## releases both lists with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var p as oracle.Pair of list of int and list of string is calling oracle.partition_results with rs
## ```
weave partition_results shard T and E with rs as list of result of T to E into Pair of list of T and list of E:
    var oks as list of T is list of T
    var errs as list of E is list of E
    for r in rs:
        if r.is_ok:
            calling oks.push with r.value
        else:
            calling errs.push with r.error
    var out as Pair of list of T and list of E with:
        set .first is oks
        set .second is errs
    return out

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Test harness: panics with `label` when `cond` is false.
weave _expect with cond as bool, label as string into void:
    if not cond:
        calling spark.panic with "oracle test failed: {label}"

## Test harness: int equality.
weave _expect_eq_int with actual as int, expected as int, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "oracle test failed: {label}: {(actual to string)} != {(expected to string)}"

## Test harness: string equality.
weave _expect_eq_string with actual as string, expected as string, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "oracle test failed: {label}: {actual} != {expected}"

## Test harness: bool equality.
weave _expect_eq_bool with actual as bool, expected as bool, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "oracle test failed: {label}"

# --- Tests ---
# Callback-driven operations are also exercised from `tests/test_oracle.py`.

test "maybe.is_some is true when a value is stored":
    var m as maybe int is some 3
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling m.is_some), true, "is_some"
test "maybe.is_some is false when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling n.is_some), false, "is_some none"
test "maybe.is_none is true when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling n.is_none), true, "is_none"
test "maybe.is_none is false when a value is stored":
    var m as maybe int is some 3
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling m.is_none), false, "is_none value"
test "maybe.unwrap returns the int payload":
    var m as maybe int is some 7
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling m.unwrap), 7, "unwrap int"
test "maybe.unwrap returns the string payload":
    var s as maybe string is some "hello"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling s.unwrap), "hello", "unwrap string"
test "maybe.unwrap_or returns the payload when present":
    var m as maybe int is some 4
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling m.unwrap_or with 0), 4, "unwrap_or"
test "maybe.unwrap_or returns the fallback when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling n.unwrap_or with 8), 8, "unwrap_or none"
test "maybe.value_or returns the payload when present":
    var m as maybe string is some "v"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling m.value_or with "x"), "v", "value_or"
test "maybe.value_or returns the fallback when empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling n.value_or with "x"), "x", "value_or none"
test "maybe.expect returns the payload":
    var m as maybe string is some "ok"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling m.expect with "failed"), "ok", "expect"
test "maybe.to_result produces ok with the payload":
    var m as maybe int is some 11
    var r as result of int to string is calling m.to_result with "missing"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling r.unwrap), 11, "to_result ok"
test "maybe.to_result produces err when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var r as result of int to string is calling n.to_result with "missing"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling r.unwrap_err), "missing", "to_result err"
test "maybe.to_list has one element when a value is stored":
    var m as maybe int is some 1
    var l as list of int is calling m.to_list
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 1, "to_list one"
test "maybe.to_list is empty without a value":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var l as list of int is calling n.to_list
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 0, "to_list zero"
test "maybe.iter is an alias of to_list":
    var m as maybe string is some "x"
    var l as list of string is calling m.iter
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 1, "iter"
test "maybe.describe renders a present value":
    var m as maybe int is some 42
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling m.describe), "some(42)", "describe"
test "maybe.describe renders an empty container":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling n.describe), "none", "describe none"
test "maybe.zip combines two present optionals":
    var a as maybe int is some 1
    var b as maybe string is some "one"
    var p as maybe Pair of int and string is calling a.zip of string with b
    if q as Pair of int and string is p:
        calling _expect_eq_int with q.first, 1, "zip first"
        calling _expect_eq_string with q.second, "one", "zip second"
test "maybe.zip is empty when one side is empty":
    var a as maybe int is some 1
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    var p as maybe Pair of int and string is calling a.zip of string with n
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling p.is_some), false, "zip none"
test "maybe.flatten re-boxes a present payload":
    var m as maybe string is some "z"
    var d as maybe string is calling m.flatten
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling d.unwrap_or with "-"), "z", "flatten"
test "maybe.flatten of an empty optional is empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    var d as maybe string is calling n.flatten
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling d.is_some), false, "flatten none"
test "maybe.or_else keeps the present payload":
    var m as maybe int is some 2
    var alt as maybe int is some 9
    var d as maybe int is calling m.or_else with alt
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling d.unwrap_or with -1), 2, "or_else"
test "maybe.or_else uses the present fallback":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var alt as maybe int is some 9
    var d as maybe int is calling n.or_else with alt
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling d.unwrap_or with -1), 9, "or_else fallback"
test "maybe.or_else of two empty optionals is empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var other as maybe int is maybe none
    var d as maybe int is calling n.or_else with other
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling d.is_some), false, "or_else empty"
test "maybe.and returns the second when both are present":
    var a as maybe string is some "a"
    var b as maybe string is some "b"
    var d as maybe string is calling a.and with b
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling d.unwrap_or with "-"), "b", "and"
test "maybe.and is empty when the second is missing":
    var a as maybe string is some "a"
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    var d as maybe string is calling a.and with n
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling d.is_some), false, "and none"
test "maybe.or returns the first when it is present":
    var a as maybe string is some "a"
    var b as maybe string is some "b"
    var d as maybe string is calling a.or with b
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling d.unwrap_or with "-"), "a", "or first"
test "maybe.or returns the second when the first is missing":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    var b as maybe string is some "b"
    var d as maybe string is calling n.or with b
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling d.unwrap_or with "-"), "b", "or second"
test "maybe.or of two empty optionals is empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    var other as maybe string is maybe none
    var d as maybe string is calling n.or with other
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling d.is_some), false, "or empty"
test "result.is_ok classifies success":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 1
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling a.is_ok), true, "is_ok"
test "result.is_ok is false for err":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling b.is_ok), false, "is_ok err"
test "result.is_err classifies an error":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling b.is_err), true, "is_err"
test "result.is_err is false for ok":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 1
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling a.is_err), false, "is_err ok"
test "result.unwrap returns the success payload":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 5
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.unwrap), 5, "unwrap"
test "result.unwrap_err returns the error":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "boom"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling b.unwrap_err), "boom", "unwrap_err"
test "result.unwrap_or returns the payload for ok":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 6
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.unwrap_or with 0), 6, "unwrap_or ok"
test "result.unwrap_or returns the fallback for err":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling b.unwrap_or with 7), 7, "unwrap_or err"
test "result.expect returns the success payload":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 9
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling a.expect with "failed"), 9, "expect"
test "result.expect_err returns the error":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "x"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling b.expect_err with "failed"), "x", "expect_err"
test "result.ok turns success into a maybe":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 3
    var m as maybe int is calling a.ok
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling m.unwrap_or with -1), 3, "ok some"
test "result.ok of an err is empty":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    var m as maybe int is calling b.ok
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling m.is_some), false, "ok err"
test "result.err exposes the error as a maybe":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    var m as maybe string is calling b.err
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling m.unwrap_or with "-"), "e", "err some"
test "result.err of an ok is empty":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 3
    var m as maybe string is calling a.err
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling m.is_some), false, "err ok"
test "result.to_maybe is an alias of ok":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 8
    var m as maybe int is calling a.to_maybe
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling m.unwrap_or with -1), 8, "to_maybe"
test "result.to_list has one element for ok":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 1
    var l as list of int is calling a.to_list
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 1, "to_list ok"
test "result.to_list is empty for err":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    var l as list of int is calling b.to_list
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 0, "to_list err"
test "result.describe formats success":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 7
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling a.describe), "ok(7)", "describe ok"
test "result.describe formats an error":
    var b as result of int to string is calling err_of with "e"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling b.describe), "err(e)", "describe err"
test "some_of boxes an int":
    var m as maybe int is calling some_of with 12
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling m.unwrap_or with 0), 12, "some_of"
test "some_of boxes a string":
    var m as maybe string is calling some_of with "text"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling m.unwrap_or with "-"), "text", "some_of string"
test "none_of with an explicit type builds an empty optional":
    var m as maybe int is calling none_of of int
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling m.is_some), false, "none_of"
test "is_some_maybe detects a present value":
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_some_maybe with (some 1)), true, "is_some_maybe"
test "is_some_maybe is false for an empty optional":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_some_maybe with n), false, "is_some_maybe none"
test "is_none_maybe detects an empty optional":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_none_maybe with n), true, "is_none_maybe"
test "is_none_maybe is false with a value":
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_none_maybe with (some 2)), false, "is_none_maybe value"
test "unwrap_maybe returns the payload":
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling unwrap_maybe with (some 21)), 21, "unwrap_maybe"
test "unwrap_or_maybe uses the present payload":
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (some 4), 0), 4, "unwrap_or_maybe"
test "unwrap_or_maybe uses the fallback when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with n, 33), 33, "unwrap_or_maybe none"
test "expect_maybe returns the payload":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling expect_maybe with (some "y"), "failed"), "y", "expect_maybe"
test "value_or_maybe uses the present payload":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling value_or_maybe with (some "a"), "z"), "a", "value_or_maybe"
test "value_or_maybe uses the fallback when empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling value_or_maybe with n, "z"), "z", "value_or_maybe none"
test "or_else_maybe prefers the first value":
    var alt as maybe int is some 9
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling or_else_maybe with (some 1), alt), -1), 1, "or_else_maybe"
test "or_else_maybe uses the fallback when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var alt as maybe int is some 9
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling or_else_maybe with n, alt), -1), 9, "or_else_maybe alt"
test "and_maybe requires both values":
    var other as maybe string is some "b"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling and_maybe with (some "a"), other), "-"), "b", "and_maybe"
test "and_maybe is empty when the second is missing":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_some_maybe with (calling and_maybe with (some "a"), n)), false, "and_maybe none"
test "or_maybe prefers the first":
    var other as maybe string is some "b"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling or_maybe with (some "a"), other), "-"), "a", "or_maybe first"
test "or_maybe uses the second when the first is missing":
    var other as maybe string is some "b"
    var empty as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling or_maybe with empty, other), "-"), "b", "or_maybe second"
test "to_result_maybe produces ok with the payload":
    var r as result of int to string is calling to_result_maybe with (some 2), "no"
    calling _expect_eq_int with (calling r.unwrap), 2, "to_result_maybe"
test "to_result_maybe produces err when empty":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var r as result of int to string is calling to_result_maybe with n, "no"
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling r.unwrap_err), "no", "to_result_maybe err"
test "to_list_maybe has one element when a value is stored":
    var l as list of int is calling to_list_maybe with (some 1)
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 1, "to_list_maybe one"
test "to_list_maybe is empty without a value":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    var l as list of int is calling to_list_maybe with n
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 0, "to_list_maybe zero"
test "describe_optional formats a present value":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling describe_optional with (some 5)), "some(5)", "describe_optional"
test "describe_optional formats an empty optional":
    var n as maybe int is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling describe_optional with n), "none", "describe_optional none"
test "iter_maybe is an alias of to_list_maybe":
    var l as list of int is calling iter_maybe with (some 1)
    calling _expect_eq_int with l.length, 1, "iter_maybe"
test "zip_maybe combines two present optionals":
    var p as maybe Pair of int and string is calling zip_maybe with (some 1), (some "u")
    if q as Pair of int and string is p:
        calling _expect_eq_int with q.first, 1, "zip_maybe first"
        calling _expect_eq_string with q.second, "u", "zip_maybe second"
test "zip_maybe is empty when one side is empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_some_maybe with (calling zip_maybe with (some 1), n)), false, "zip_maybe none"
test "flatten_maybe re-boxes the payload":
    calling _expect_eq_string with (calling unwrap_or_maybe with (calling flatten_maybe with (some "k")), "-"), "k", "flatten_maybe"
test "flatten_maybe of an empty optional is empty":
    var n as maybe string is maybe none
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_some_maybe with (calling flatten_maybe with n)), false, "flatten_maybe none"
test "is_ok_result classifies success":
    var a as result of int to string is calling ok_of with 1
    calling _expect_eq_bool with (calling is_ok_result with a), true, "is_ok_result"
test "is_ok_result is false for err":
